WEBVTT

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.320
Tashiro!

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.320
Now...

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.970
Brondis!

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:37.990
What?

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.400
I knew it... It's Miura.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:06.870
<i>With this,</i>

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.600
<i>people will think he's a passerby 
who, startled by the sound, fell.</i>

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.390
<i>I can't let the police arrest him.</i>

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:20.720
<i>Turning him into a criminal 
won't solve anything!</i>

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:59.900
<b>Twelfth Haunting 
I'm Going to the Future</b>

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.340
Tashiro... Hey, Tashiro!

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.860
Ow...

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.530
Huh? Inaba?

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.680
You okay?

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.000
It felt like something hit me on the head!

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.120
And I fell over and heard this huge noise!

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.830
<i>Good, she didn't see Miura's face.</i>

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.430
Wh-What was that? What happened?

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.950
Ow...

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.140
It might have been a gas explosion.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.790
The police will be here soon.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:28.510
Hey! Another person is here!

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.470
Wake up!

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.580
I heard it was a gas explosion.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.050
Oh, dear...

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.030
Splendid, master...

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.070
To use the Petits so masterfully...

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.990
What are you talking about, Fool?

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.500
Weren't you the one who said, "Now"?

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.790
No.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.160
That was the echo of your heart.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.230
The echo of my heart?

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.580
Indeed!

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:06.750
We resonated in response to your desire.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.310
I don't get it.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.100
Someday, you'll be able 
to feel it more clearly!

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:17.180
That won't do me any good.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:22.320
Are you sure? It is very helpful.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.540
For example...

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:31.450
It seems someone with a very powerful 
spiritual aura is at the apartments.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.040
Croquette on rice! So good!

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.700
Ruriko-san is the best!

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:41.580
I'm back!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.500
Oh, Yushi-kun. Welcome back.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.800
Akine-san, you're back!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.720
Yeah. I'm back.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.970
I see...

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:55.040
That must have been hard.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:59.950
The id monster has finally started 
to control Miura-sensei, huh?

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.090
How awful!

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.820
But you did great, Yushi-kun!

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.540
Your quick choice to defend Miura-sensei...

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.740
It isn't his fault he got possessed, is it?

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:12.330
No.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.150
So I wonder if there's a way to save him.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:19.340
I mean, I actually can't do 
anything on my own.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:23.580
But it doesn't feel like a coincidence.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:24.830
So...

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:30.830
By "coincidence," that strong misogyny 
built up in the tiny room at JTB.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.350
By "coincidence," Miura-sensei came to JTB.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:41.230
And by "coincidence," Miura-sensei's 
heart was emptied by women.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:44.630
This all seems too much for mere coincidence.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:49.660
Yes, perhaps this is Miura-sensei's fate...

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.330
Fate...

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.090
If that's the case,

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:57.670
then maybe our fate is to save him.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.500
Akine-san!

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.130
But why, do you think, 
was he after Tashiro-chan?

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:06.090
That's because...

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:10.010
It was partly that Miura 
saw us together, but...

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.850
Mostly, Tashiro stands out as a woman.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:18.290
I think she's an attractive girl, 
objectively speaking.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.640
Even around men, she's cheerful and friendly.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.270
She'd probably be popular anywhere.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.700
Yes.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.700
But from the perspective of 
one who isn't that way,

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:34.940
more than anything else, she'd provoke 
jealousy and irritation...

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:38.610
Especially in someone who hates women.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.850
"Look at that bitch, sucking up to men!"

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:44.170
That's probably what he's thinking.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.580
A-Akine-san...

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.130
Harsh, Akine-chan.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.420
Scared?

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.510
But people like that do exist.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.430
<i>For a second there, she was like Hase.</i>

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:01.400
And those feelings tied the 
id monster to Miura-sensei.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:07.190
That's why it's decided on 
Tashiro-chan as its first victim.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.490
The first of many to come.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.440
What will happen to Miura after this?

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:13.880
Hmm...

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:18.100
His mind will gradually be devoured, I think.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.770
Externally, he'll appear to be mentally ill.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:25.780
But the police and doctors 
won't know the real cause.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.770
I... want to do something!

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.930
Before that happens to Miura.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:38.290
By coincidence, my fate brought 
me to the Yokai Apartments...

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.580
And to the Petits.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.390
<b>Oranges</b>

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:47.270
By coincidence, the id monster took 
over Miura at his new school.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.190
If this is fate,

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:54.450
then my meeting Miura was also fate.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.400
<i>That's right...</i>

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:01.580
<i>There's still time.</i>

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:05.720
<i>Before Miura disappears!</i>

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:10.940
<i>I don't want anyone else to get hurt!</i>

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:16.050
<b>Katsumasa Miura</b>

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:16.050
Thank you for coming, Inaba.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:19.480
You're here on behalf of the students?

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.970
That makes me happy.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.260
Of course.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.900
I guess I left the hospital 
and wandered around.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.500
I caused problems for everyone, huh?

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.560
Sensei, you're tired.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.700
Everyone was just surprised.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:36.620
I'm really sorry!

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:38.030
Inaba!

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.370
Tashiro...

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.400
I'm going to make a call on the roof.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.330
I can't do it here, can I?

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.350
N-No.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:57.800
Inaba, could you get a vase 
from the nurse's station?

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.900
I don't want those flowers to die.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:01.610
Right...

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:02.560
Thanks.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.950
Damn you, girl...

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.070
Damn you, girl!

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.340
I'll kill you!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:35.090
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.980
You bitch...

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:42.150
All girls need to die!

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:54.630
The bugs are

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.060
being sucked away!

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:08.670
This is... shikigami magic?

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:13.800
Akine-san?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.680
<i>Onwabira unken sowaka!</i>

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:29.520
Stepping on demons is one way to seal them.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:32.310
Now, it won't be able to leave.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.270
I see, I see.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:37.610
Then, it was absorbed into a greater vessel.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.340
That's right!

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:42.770
I just have to get Fujiyuki-sensei 
to dispose of this.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.030
<i>That looked exactly like 
the real-life Tashiro!</i>

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.750
<i>Spiritualists are amazing!</i>

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.680
Miura-sensei...

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:56.050
Where am I?

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.470
It's all over, Miura-sensei.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.360
I'm sure you're confused,

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.390
but you can forget about everything.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:08.190
Get better soon, and return to school.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.810
Sensei, isn't that great?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:12.410
Now, let's get you back to your room.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.200
What?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:24.310
What do you mean, forget about everything?

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.370
It isn't that simple.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:30.200
You don't know what I've been through.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:34.030
I didn't study so hard to go through that!

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:36.380
I... I...

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:39.800
That isn't right!

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.390
Ophelia loves Hamlet more than anything.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.900
Show more emotion!

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.560
It'll help the audience get invested.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.230
Miura-sensei,

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:57.940
our school's done Hamlet this way for years.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:01.450
You can do that when you're older.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.010
You're in high school, so be more easygoing.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:05.870
That's how you should do it.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.520
What's with that teacher?

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.210
He's new, isn't he?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.630
He thinks he's in a position 
to tell us what to do?

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:18.560
Let's teach him a lesson.

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:20.840
It wasn't my fault.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.510
I've always been excellent!

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.680
Those kids lied...

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:30.680
"Creepy"? "Sexual harassment"? 
"A perverted teacher"?

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:33.560
D-Damn them all!

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:37.820
It wasn't my fault...

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.020
It wasn't!

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:40.660
Sensei...

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:45.680
All they had to do was shut 
up and do as I said!

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:48.080
And then, those damn girls...

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.910
Who... Who did they think they were?

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.450
Damn it!

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:54.220
Hey—

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:55.160
Yushi-kun.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:58.010
We're leaving.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.050
Akine-san...

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.970
I don't understand...

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.380
What did I do wrong?!

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.820
I did my best!

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:12.770
I did my best...

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.840
Morning, Inaba!

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.140
Morning.

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:32.870
Is your head okay?

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.800
Just fine. Ow...

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:37.790
Jeez, what are you doing?

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:39.850
By the way, did you hear?

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:42.380
Miura-sensei went to the hospital.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.490
Then, English today will be study hall!

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.490
Yes!

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.380
And I can take a great nap!

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:50.800
Don't you sleep, even when 
the teacher's there?

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.610
You could tell?

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.330
<i>I was wrong...</i>

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:58.980
<i>Even though the id monster's gone,</i>

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.540
<i>it doesn't make Miura a good person.</i>

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.730
<i>It just makes him the person he was.</i>

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:08.540
<i>Even if he's a bad adult, with no 
idea what he's done wrong,</i>

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.290
<i>that's who he is.</i>

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:14.330
<i>I can't deny that, can I?</i>

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:17.170
What are you thinking about, Inaba?

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.240
Nothing...

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:22.630
That sounds suspicious.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.730
Worry about yourself, not others.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:28.800
From now on, no walking around late at night!

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.220
Ow!

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.550
Inaba hit me!

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:35.890
<i>It's over, right?</i>

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.020
<i>Now, it's back to normal life.</i>

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.730
<b>Come to the Art Room at Lunch</b>

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:45.900
What's this?

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.820
<b>Come to the Art Room at Lunch</b>

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.240
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.410
Huh? Where's Inaba?

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.410
No idea.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.160
<b>Art Room</b>

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.410
<i>What? No one's here.</i>

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.460
<i>Someone's idea of a joke?</i>

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.340
<i>I thought it was those punks from before.</i>

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:13.200
M-Miura?

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.360
What are you thinking?!

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:21.080
I know... I know.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:24.300
But I can't help it now.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:29.700
This is the only way I can feel better!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:34.730
It feels like I'd be better off if 
I just destroy everything...

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.180
Right?

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:38.250
Don't you think so, too?

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:41.420
Are you stupid? That's just running away!

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.830
If you're an adult, face things!

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.170
Me? I'm not running...

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.340
Why would you say that?

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:51.470
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:52.710
<i>He's all messed up!</i>

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:57.250
You idiot!

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.120
Brondis!

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:09.650
Damn it! My left shoulder...

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.490
Are you all right, master?

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:15.870
At times like this, call Goyelems.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.700
Goyelems?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.110
Power...

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:20.580
Goyelems!

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:26.670
Goyelems... A doll made of stone.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:32.010
I'm saved.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.120
<i>Miura,</i>

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.750
<i>you really are sick.</i>

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.730
<i>Go get treated at the hospital.</i>

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:46.510
<i>Everyone fails, in all kinds of ways.</i>

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.240
<i>But why give up there?</i>

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.740
An explosion in the art room?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.070
Sensei, this way!

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.520
<i>You can't change the past.</i>

00:16:55.860 --> 00:17:00.490
<i>So you have to figure out how to avoid 
making the same mistake again!</i>

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.350
<i>But...</i>

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:07.030
<i>This time, it's really over.</i>

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:19.040
But, Fool, can you do 
something about Brondis?

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.060
Like what?

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:22.670
Make it a little more effective.

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:24.660
Or concentrated.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:27.270
If this happens every time I use it...

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:33.570
You will simply have to learn 
to control your power!

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:36.950
We can do nothing about that!

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:39.760
Yushi-kun...

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.930
What happened to you?

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:44.300
Are you all right?

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:45.410
Ryu-san...

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:50.600
I see... That must have been rough.

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:53.840
No, getting involved was my choice.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:58.470
But I don't know if I was able to save him.

00:17:58.980 --> 00:18:01.110
Some people can't be saved.

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:07.100
That's right.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:10.400
When you scoop water, 
no matter how big your hands,

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.110
it drips from the gaps.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:15.550
Supposedly, Buddha's hands have webbing,

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.960
and water would probably drip from his, too.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:19.160
Isshiki-san...

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:25.330
All we can do is think about the 
water still in our hands.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:29.640
But that doesn't mean we don't 
care about the water lost

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:31.750
or that we should give up.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:37.230
You can't touch some things in this 
world, even if you're next to them.

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:41.180
And sometimes, you're offered a hand 
from a place you never expected.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.600
That is karma.

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:46.980
Karma, huh?

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.890
Sometimes, the answer may 
take a while to come.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:50.770
Ryu-san...

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:52.480
<i>That's right.</i>

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:55.370
<i>Even someone with his power couldn't stop</i>

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.450
<i>two hundred people from killing themselves.</i>

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:03.400
<i>The hostages he saved were 
connected to him by karma.</i>

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:07.120
<i>And the two hundred who died 
were the water that fell.</i>

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:09.810
<i>I'm sure he wanted to save both groups.</i>

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:12.320
<i>But sometimes, you can't do it.</i>

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.240
<i>That's reality.</i>

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:20.970
<i>The reality we have to face and overcome.</i>

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:25.080
You guys are all so gloomy...

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:28.310
Yushi, eat these and cheer up.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:37.070
So sweet!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:39.470
They're really good!

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.910
Ruriko-san, more sea urchin and tuna!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.530
I got these fresh.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.790
They taste better fresh, right?

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:52.030
I didn't like sea urchin, 
but this is really good!

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:53.820
I could eat a ton!

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.300
This is karma, too.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.280
What's this sound?

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.300
What's Hase doing here?

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:10.980
Oh, he called a while ago, and I accidentally
 told him about Miura-sensei.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:13.980
Inaba!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:16.020
H-Hey...

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:17.770
What were you thinking?!

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:19.740
I told you not to get involved!

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:24.160
Akine-san, train this idiot 
harder and level him up!

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:26.240
This idiot...

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.580
Love hurts, huh?

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:30.860
Yushi looks like a chestnut, chirp.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:32.870
No, more like a bean jam bun, chirp.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.750
Both are all swollen, chirp!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:40.610
Reality is harsh...

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:46.930
<i>And a month later,</i>

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.650
<i>my wounds had healed a lot.</i>

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:53.150
Don't glare and then ignore us!

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:55.580
Well, our forgiveness won't cost much.

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.040
We're going to karaoke!

00:20:58.040 --> 00:20:59.730
But we're a little short.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:03.150
<i>And my normal life returned.</i>

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:06.010
What will you do, master?

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:08.320
Use Brondis?

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.490
Or Hippogriff?

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:15.750
Okay, Fool...

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:16.980
We're running!

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.840
Let's run!

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.750
Wait!

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:29.000
<i>It will take millions of yen to repair 
the art room I destroyed.</i>

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.600
<i>I feel bad.</i>

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:34.980
<i>Once I graduate, I'll donate 
to repair it, little by little.</i>

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.590
<i>Yes, of course.</i>

00:23:11.270 --> 00:23:14.950
With all that stuff over, 
time for summer break!

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:16.230
I can't wait!

00:23:16.230 --> 00:23:18.400
You're so excited, Yushi-kun.

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:20.630
Akine-chan was excited, too.

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:24.380
She said she could train you 
hard over summer break.

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:26.040
Seriously?

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:27.520
I can't wait!

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:31.050
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:32.340
Metamorphosis.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:32.340
<b>Thirteenth Haunting 
Metamorphosis</b>

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:34.200
Wh-What is this?

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:36.190
What's happened to me?
